    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Fracture aperture plays an important role in controlling fluid flow through fractures. However, it is a parameter which is difficult to measure. This paper discusses the aperture scaling law for a smooth fracture, a fractal fracture and fractal fracture networks. It is found that the fracture aperture can be linearly scaled with respect to the effective stress, fracture length and material properties for a smooth fracture. The aperture also depends on the fractal dimension of the rough surfaces for a fractal fracture and decreases with increasing the fractal dimension. For a fractal fracture network, the distribution of fracture apertures can be determined if the fracture length -frequency relationship and the fractal dimension are known.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
